  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "About three hundred years before the San Cha Mountain opening, Wu clan exterminated Wang clan but missed three children. The eldest was eight. Those survivors later entered an ancient rank six Gu Immortal inheritance, cultivated to rank five, and wiped out Wu clan in three days. He summoned an army of hounds that engulfed Wu clan village. After revenge they lived in seclusion until their inheritances appeared. Entering the yellow pillar requires refining rank one dog enslavement Gu. Talk credits him with at least three rank five dog enslavement Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        324
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "fac_wu_clan",
        "fac_wang_clan",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "gu_dog_enslavement_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "No chapter describes his appearance.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Among the three kings, King Quan was an enslavement path Gu Master, and the inheritance is built to favor that path.",
      "chapters": [
        347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "enslavement-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan tells Bai Ning Bing that the last few rounds of King Quan Inheritance hold a large group of lion mastiffs, mutated beasts that were King Quan’s trump cards, and two dog emperors that were his left and right arms, each able to match a rank five Gu Master.",
      "chapters": [
        387
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-trump-cards",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_bai_ning_bing",
        "inh_king_quan_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo Wu Tian names King Quan as Wang Er Gou, and says he had two dog emperors, Ying Ming and Ba Huang.",
      "chapters": [
        391
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
